    "sentence_translations": [
      "Tiangou eats the sun",
      "",
      "We all know solar eclipses are natural events.",
      "When the moon passes between the sun and the earth and blocks the sunrays, ..",
      ".. we won’t be able to see the sun or just see some parts of the sun.",
      "",
      "However, in ancient China people didn’t understand this fact.",
      "People believed the solar eclipse meant a giant heavenly dog was eating the sun, ..",
      ".. and the lunar eclipse meant the heavenly dog ate the moon.",
      "Therefore, when an eclipse occurred people would run outside to rescue the sun or the moon.",
      "They would play drums and gongs or set off firecrackers to scare away the dog.",
      "Even today, people in some villages keep this traditional custom during eclipses.",
      ""
